<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Token Radar — pre-token protocols ranked by implied launch value</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="shell">
  <header class="top">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">TOKEN RADAR · MAKE.FUN BOUNTY</p>
      <h1>Which protocol launches the next big token?</h1>
      <p class="lede">200 pre-token protocols, ranked by what a token would be worth if their
      record stayed as it is. Click any row for the value breakdown and a farm plan.
      Protocols whose token already trades are listed separately, at their real market cap.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stats" id="stats"></div>
  </header>

  <section class="method" aria-label="How the value is worked out">
    <h2>How the implied value is worked out</h2>
    <p><b>implied = 10^(0.92 · log10 TVL) × growth × age × chains × sector × 0.70</b></p>
    <p>Growth is the 7-day TVL change (unreported counts as flat). Age is days since first
    listing, capped at 4 years — a protocol that has run for years with no token is more likely
    to issue one. Chains adds 8% per extra chain, capped at 6. Sector is a per-category
    multiplier (Lending 1.18, DEX 1.15, down to Bridge 0.85). Nothing is hardcoded by name:
    the same formula scores every protocol. Snapshot date and floor are shown in the header.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="controls">
    <label>Search <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Name or slug…" autocomplete="off"></label>
    <label>Chain <select id="chain"><option value="">All chains</option></select></label>
    <label>Category <select id="cat"><option value="">All categories</option></select></label>
    <label>List <select id="tab">
      <option value="board">Pre-token board (200)</option>
      <option value="live">Already trading (24)</option>
    </select></label>
    <span class="count" id="count"></span>
  </div>

  <section id="detail" class="detail" hidden></section>

  <table class="board">
    <thead><tr id="head"></tr></thead>
    <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="foot">Values are the radar's own claim from the sealed snapshot — not a prediction
  that a token will launch, or when. Farm only money you can afford to leave in place.</p>
</div>
<script src="../data.js"></script>
<script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```
